<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Ancalites</h1><p class="st-meta">54 BCE – 54 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">British people named once by Julius Caesar among those who surrendered to him in 54 BCE, leading him to the stronghold of Cassivellaunus.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Ancalites are known only from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commentarii-de-bello-gallico">Caesar's Gallic War</a>. In 54 BCE they were among five British peoples, alongside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/iceni">Cenimagni</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/segontiaci">Segontiaci</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bibroci">Bibroci</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cassi">Cassi</a>, who sent embassies to submit after the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trinovantes">Trinovantes</a> had won his protection.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Caesar</a> says that from these envoys he learned the location of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassivellaunus">Cassivellaunus's</a> stronghold, protected by woods and marshes, which he then stormed. Beyond this, nothing is recorded of their rulers, settlements or customs, and their territory is uncertain, though the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-thames">Thames</a> valley has been suggested.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>No later source mentions the Ancalites. They were probably absorbed by stronger neighbours such as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/catuvellauni">Catuvellauni</a> or the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/atrebates-britain">Atrebates (Britain)</a> in the century before the Roman conquest of 43.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 54 BCE – 54 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:58.63%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>54 BCE – 54 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Common Brittonic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-54&amp;focus=ancalites" aria-label="Ancalites on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4633 314 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ancalites lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4953 570h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4953 570h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United Kingdom. <a href="/atlas?year=-54&amp;focus=ancalites">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

